        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "There are signs that our society is beginning to move in that direction. Online retailers are touting their minimalist packaging, and “right to repair” legislation, which would require manufacturers to make the tools and parts needed to repair their products available to third parties, has now been proposed in seventeen states. The reduce and repair movements are still in their infancies, but so was the recycling movement at that first Earth Day in 1970.",
            "block_bbox": [
